<p>In the latest turn in the Iran-Israel-U.S. war, U.S. forces struck military sites on Iran&#x27;s Kharg Island on March 14, expanding the campaign to an island that handles about 90% of Iran&#x27;s oil exports and sits near the Strait of Hormuz. President Trump said the strikes had &quot;totally demolished&quot; most of the island and warned that more attacks could follow, while Iranian officials threatened energy infrastructure in the region linked to U.S. companies. The move matters well beyond the battlefield. Kharg is both a fortified military position and Iran&#x27;s main crude export terminal, so damage there could tighten global oil supply and push prices higher. The escalation also spread across Gulf energy routes: sources cited by Dawn said some loading operations were suspended in Fujairah in the United Arab Emirates after a strike there, and the U.S. embassy in Baghdad urged Americans to leave Iraq as the conflict entered its third week, with more than 2,000 people reported killed since Feb. 28.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/BKitwse6ZTFbvTZsz59eqDuoaUrqYHKYyALo3F21PyawISYXbh7sHjYqwo7PZ4ucsyMCZVlG5tBpg63fAvGBgXjzTTJ3XGE46unA6UPzmpoJIqZFaCVr6h4UxAGyofjanL_W4dzYv4kjJi_GQ2YxP-hbtzV5SNPzqaA7d7YT6X7gdpl01nvXMiAD4el7WEWL6-k0JDvuHNR7EITt2MNhAxk2aKWhyQ' alt='Smoke billowing from a flare stack at the Port of Kharg Island oil terminal in Iran in 2017.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Island chain: Iran&#x27;s offshore islands have strategic value because they anchor oil terminals, shipping lanes, and military surveillance across the Persian Gulf, making them both valuable targets and key defensive positions.</li><li>Hormuz security: President Trump said warships from several countries would help guard the Strait of Hormuz, the narrow maritime chokepoint linking the Gulf to the Arabian Sea.</li><li>Regional warning: Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi said Tehran would attack any regional energy infrastructure tied to an American company if those facilities were hit, widening concerns for Gulf-based operators.</li><li>Civilian toll: An air strike on a refrigerator and heater factory in Isfahan killed at least 15 people on Saturday, according to Iran&#x27;s semi-official Fars news agency, as cited by Dawn.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: Trump said U.S. strikes had &quot;totally demolished&quot; most of Kharg Island and signaled that additional attacks were still possible. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-says-us-strikes-demolished-irans-kharg-island-warns-of-more-attacks/article70745798.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Iranian military: An Iranian military spokesperson urged people in the UAE to leave ports, docks, and what he called &quot;American hideouts&quot; after saying U.S. forces had targeted Iranian islands. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1982253/war-escalates-as-us-strikes-irans-energy-lifeline'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>News analysis outlets: Several explanatory reports described Kharg not just as a battlefield target but as the economic heart of Iran&#x27;s oil export system, underscoring why even limited disruption there can reverberate globally. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/14/world/middleeast/kharg-island-iran-oil-us-trump.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/World/Middle-East/2026/0314/iran-war-kharg-island-us-bahrain-oil-drone-attack'>What to know about Iran’s islands, as the US expands its bombing campaign there</a> - csmonitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1982253/war-escalates-as-us-strikes-irans-energy-lifeline'>War escalates as US strikes Iran’s energy lifeline</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/14/world/middleeast/kharg-island-iran-oil-us-trump.html'>What to Know About Kharg Island, Iran’s Key Oil Hub</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.youtube.com/shorts/G3biH7PbBaY'>🇮🇷 Why did the #US military bomb the strategic 